<onlyinclude>A '''neural processing unit''' ('''NPU''') is a specialized computing accelerator designed to execute selected neural-network operations efficiently. Typical implementations emphasize parallel multiply–accumulate arithmetic and controlled movement of model weights, activations, and intermediate results. The term describes a class of accelerators, not a universal instruction set, precision standard, or guarantee of performance.</onlyinclude>

